CORE
table.c
--object-bits 12
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
The flags (- + space # 0), field width and precision (also given as *), the
length modifiers hh, h, l, ll, j, z and t, integer minima and maxima, and %c,
%s and %% give the output and the result of glibc, both for a buffer that
holds the whole output and for one that truncates it. On Windows, the
test needs more than the 256 objects of the default --object-bits.
